<<<
mortifiedly. A bad form; see -EDLY.

mortify. For inflexions see VERBS IN -IE, -Y, -YE, 6.

mortise, -ice. The first is better. In m. & tenon, the m. is the receiving cavity.
===
**mortifiedly.** A bad form; see ^^-EDLY^^.

**mortify.** For inflexions see ^^VERBS IN -IE, -Y, -YE^^, 6.

**mortise, -ice.** The first is better. In *m. & tenon*, the m. is the receiving cavity.
>>>

<<<
moslem, muslim. The OED treats the first as the ordinary English form, & there is no doubt that it is so. Correction into muslim is to be deprecated; see Dipacticism. M. ean be used as adjective or as noun, & the plural of the noun is preferably -ms, but sometimes the same as the singular; the use of the plural moslemin or muslimin is bad didacticism. See also MUSSULMAN.
===
**moslem, muslim.** The OED treats the first as the ordinary English form, & there is no doubt that it is so. Correction into *muslim* is to be deprecated; see ^^DIDACTICISM^^. *M.* can be used as adjective or as noun, & the plural of the noun is preferably *-ms*, but sometimes the same as the singular; the use of the plural *moslemin* or *muslimin* is bad didacticism. See also ^^MUSSULMAN^^.
>>>

<<<
mosquito. Pl. -os; see -o(z)s 6.

-most. The commoner words with this ending are best pronounced -ost, not -dst, though mistaken effort is often expended on satisfying the supposed demands of the spelling. The origin was not the word most, but a double superlative suffix -mest, & it is not unlikely that the ordinary colloquial pronunciation records this fact. Foremost, innermost, uppermost, topmost, inmost, utmost, hindermost, are examples of the words in which the obscure o is better than the clear 6,
===
**mosquito.** Pl. *-os*; see ^^-O(E)S^^ 6.

**-most.** The commoner words with this ending are best pronounced *-ost*, not *-ōst*, though mistaken effort is often expended on satisfying the supposed demands of the spelling. The origin was not the word *most*, but a double superlative suffix *-mest*, & it is not unlikely that the ordinary colloquial pronunciation records this fact. *Foremost, innermost, uppermost, topmost, inmost, utmost, hindermost,* are examples of the words in which the obscure *o* is better than the clear *ō*.
>>>

<<<
most(ly). The internecine conflict
===
**most(ly).** *The internecine conflict*
>>>
